WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.590
Every pursuit starts on SAM.gov.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.780
Rhodo monitors new federal opportunities with the filters set

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.340
for your firm, pulls in the solicitation documents,

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.360
and analyzes each one against your capabilities.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.600
So you start with work that fits, and a clear reason why.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.520
Those opportunities land in your pipeline.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.240
You can see what’s been analyzed, what’s moving into proposal

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.720
preparation, and what’s been submitted.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.100
Deadlines and fit scores show you where to focus.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.420
Open a pursuit to see the AI’s analysis.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.760
It reads the solicitation, pulls out the requirements,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.580
and compares them with your firm’s experience.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.440
You get a bid recommendation, with the strengths

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.760
and gaps laid out for your review.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.870
In Selection, Rhodo recommends past projects from your firm’s records,

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.490
each with the experience that supports it.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.970
Then it recommends the people whose qualifications

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.490
fit each role.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.630
Accept the team, or compare an alternative.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.910
Those choices build your experience matrix,

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.530
connecting people to the projects they delivered.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.690
Approve it, and the selection moves forward.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.590
From there, Rhodo drafts resumes,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.670
project sheets, and narratives.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:20.010
The solicitation, amendments, and generated sections stay side by side,

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.650
so you can check the source against the output.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:27.950
The Proposal tab brings every section into one SF330 package.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.790
See what’s ready, fill any gaps,

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.570
and give it your final review.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.390
Want something changed?

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.930
Just tell the assistant.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.770
Rhodo saves your feedback on tone, terminology,

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:44.190
and how you describe your work, and uses it to guide future drafts.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.290
Your pursue and decline decisions sharpen the scoring, too.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.170
So with every pursuit, the writing sounds more like your team.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.110
Behind it all is your firm’s knowledge base:

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.570
past projects, personnel and their qualifications,

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.030
and the partner firms you team with.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.610
New files come in through Documents,

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.510
where you upload records and follow their processing.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.310
That’s Rhodo.

00:02:08.596 --> 00:02:12.530
Monitoring, analysis, matching, and proposal preparation,

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.690
handled for you, with your team in control of every decision.
